  "note": "A watch voice note surviving a round-trip through an unmodified Readest. The audio pointer, the duration and the transcript provenance are server-owned: they go out on the wire under hb-prefixed keys so a modified client can show a play button, and they are re-attached on the way back in. Readest's own upsert path never sends them, so without the re-attach the first sync from the desktop would quietly turn a voice note into a plain one. Editing the transcript text by hand promotes it from asr to human; leaving it alone does not.",
